virgl gdi: an allocation for a texture without guest storage still has a size

A multisampled texture lives on the host only: the virgl driver gives it no storage in the
guest and asks the winsys for a resource of size zero. On Windows a resource is an
allocation, and Windows refuses one of no size (D3DKMTCreateAllocation, invalid parameter),
so no multisampled render target or depth buffer could be made.

Such an allocation is now one byte, the size textures that are filled through staging
buffers already get. `tools/win7-hello/d3d9msaa.c` makes them.

---
--- a/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/gdi/virgl_gdi_winsys.c
+++ b/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/gdi/virgl_gdi_winsys.c
@@ -218,7 +218,10 @@
    AllocExchange.ResourceOptions.last_level = last_level;
    AllocExchange.ResourceOptions.nr_samples = nr_samples;
    AllocExchange.ResourceOptions.flags = flags;
-   AllocExchange.Size = size;
+   /* moose-ripple: a multisampled texture has no storage in the guest
+    * (virgl_resource_layout gives it no size), and Windows refuses an allocation
+    * of no size. One byte, as textures filled through staging buffers get. */
+   AllocExchange.Size = size ? size : 1;
 
    struct gdikmt_createallocation CreateAllocation;
    D3DDDI_ALLOCATIONINFO AllocationInfo;
